"heading","depth":2,"id":"a-child-component-rejects-the-form-input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A child component rejects the form input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for reusable base options and derive the input type with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularFormType"},{"type":"text","value":". This keeps the child compatible when the parent adds\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { AngularFormType } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { firstName: '', age: 0 },\n})\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-profile-fields',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<!-- fields -->`,\n})\nexport class ProfileFieldsComponent {\n  form = input.required<AngularFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>>()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"async-defaults-do-not-update","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Async defaults do not update"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":" receives its initial options when the component is constructed.\nWhen data arrives later, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.reset(nextValues)"},{"type":"text","value":" deliberately, normally\ninside an Angular "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect"},{"type":"text","value":", or resolve the data before constructing the form.\nGuard against replacing edits the user has already made."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"injectform-reports-a-missing-injection-context","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":" reports a missing injection context"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectForm"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectSelector"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectField"},{"type":"text","value":" in an Angular injection\ncontext, such as a component field initializer or constructor. Do not call\nthem later from an event handler, subscription callback, or arbitrary utility\nfunction."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type instantiation is excessively deep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form issue tracker"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Include\nthe Angular and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors exist but are not displayed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" respects the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" policy. Inspect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.handleBlur()"},{"type":"text","value":" if the policy depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBlurred"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"an-input-initially-renders-undefined","text":"An input initially renders undefined","level":2},{"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","text":"A field value is unknown","level":2},{"id":"a-child-component-rejects-the-form-input","text":"A child component rejects the form input","level":2},{"id":"async-defaults-do-not-update","text":"Async defaults do not update","level":2},{"id":"injectform-reports-a-missing-injection-context","text":"injectForm reports a missing injection context","level":2},{"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","text":"Type instantiation is excessively deep","level":2},{"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","text":"Errors exist but are not displayed","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page covers common Angular and TypeScript problems when using TanStack\nForm.\n\n## An input initially renders `undefined`\n\nEvery value rendered by an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from\nthe first render.\n\n```ts\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable fields or\nsupply a complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nform = injectForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## A child component rejects the form input\n\nUse `formOptions` for reusable base options and derive the input type with\n`AngularFormType`. This keeps the child compatible when the parent adds\n`onSubmit`:\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { AngularFormType } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { firstName: '', age: 0 },\n})\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-profile-fields',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<!-- fields -->`,\n})\nexport class ProfileFieldsComponent {\n  form = input.required<AngularFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>>()\n}\n```\n\n## Async defaults do not update\n\n`injectForm` receives its initial options when the component is constructed.\nWhen data arrives later, call `form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately, normally\ninside an Angular `effect`, or resolve the data before constructing the form.\nGuard against replacing edits the user has already made.\n\n## `injectForm` reports a missing injection context\n\nCall `injectForm`, `injectSelector`, and `injectField` in an Angular injection\ncontext, such as a component field initializer or constructor. Do not call\nthem later from an event handler, subscription callback, or arbitrary utility\nfunction.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe Angular and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.api.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.api.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.api.handleBlur()` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debugging\ntitle: Debugging Angular Usage\n---\n\nThis page covers common Angular and TypeScript problems when using TanStack\nForm.\n\n## An input initially renders `undefined`\n\nEvery value rendered by an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from\nthe first render.\n\n```ts\nform = injectForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable fields or\nsupply a complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nform = injectForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form and\nfield groups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## A child component rejects the form input\n\nUse `formOptions` for reusable base options and derive the input type with\n`AngularFormType`. This keeps the child compatible when the parent adds\n`onSubmit`:\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { formOptions } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\nimport type { AngularFormType } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\nexport const profileFormOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { firstName: '', age: 0 },\n})\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-profile-fields',\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<!-- fields -->`,\n})\nexport class ProfileFieldsComponent {\n  form = input.required<AngularFormType<typeof profileFormOptions>>()\n}\n```\n\n## Async defaults do not update\n\n`injectForm` receives its initial options when the component is constructed.\nWhen data arrives later, call `form.reset(nextValues)` deliberately, normally\ninside an Angular `effect`, or resolve the data before constructing the form.\nGuard against replacing edits the user has already made.\n\n## `injectForm` reports a missing injection context\n\nCall `injectForm`, `injectSelector`, and `injectField` in an Angular injection\ncontext, such as a component field initializer or constructor. Do not call\nthem later from an event handler, subscription callback, or arbitrary utility\nfunction.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe Angular and TypeScript versions, the form value type, and the smallest\nfailing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.api.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.api.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.api.handleBlur()` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n"}
